B.RK=s(["restraint","extravagance","optimism","indecision"],t.s)
B.a_d=new A.bx("Although the novelist's early works were dismissed by critics as overly sentimental, her later novels, with their spare prose and unflinching portraits of rural poverty, earned her a reputation for ______ that few of her contemporaries could match.",u.Y,B.RK,'"spare prose" (ortiqchasiz uslub) va "unflinching" (hissiyotga berilmay) \u2014 yozuvchi o\'zini tutib yozadi \u2192 restraint (vazminlik). "Although" erta asarlardagi "sentimental" uslubga qarama-qarshilikni ko\'rsatadi.')
B.R_=s(["irreversible","observable","unprecedented","gradual"],t.s)
B.a_k=new A.bx("Marine biologists warn that the decline of many coral reefs is serious, but they insist it is not ______: with sharp cuts in emissions and strong local protection, many reefs could recover within a few decades.",u.Y,B.R_,'Gapning davomi: "could recover" \u2014 tiklanishi mumkin. Demak, jarayon qaytarib bo\'lmaydigan (irreversible) emas.')
B.Sx=s(["ignores","corrects","extends","praises"],t.s)
B.a_s=new A.bx("Critics of historian Karim Nazarov claim that he ______ earlier scholarship on medieval trade, but in fact his study builds directly on those findings, even as it corrects several of their assumptions.",u.Y,B.Sx,'"but in fact ... builds directly on those findings" \u2014 tanqidchilarning fikri bunga zid bo\'lishi kerak: u avvalgi ishlarni e\'tiborsiz qoldiradi (ignores). "corrects" va "extends" \u2014 u haqiqatan ham shunday qiladi, zidlik yo\'q.')
B.Ri=s(["efficient","ornate","fragile","controversial"],t.s)
B.a_O=new A.bx("The new bridge design is remarkably ______: engineers assembled its prefabricated sections in just eleven days, a fraction of the time required for a conventional bridge of similar size.",u.Y,B.Ri,"Ikki nuqtadan keyingi tushuntirish \u2014 juda tez qurildi \u2192 efficient (samarali).")
B.Rq=s(["arbitrary","vivid","traditional","precise"],t.s)
B.a_o=new A.bx("Some readers find the poet's imagery ______, but careful study reveals that each seemingly random image is connected to the collection's central theme of migration.",u.Y,B.Rq,"\"seemingly random\" (tasodifiy ko'rinadigan) \u2192 arbitrary (o'zboshimchalik bilan tanlangan, tartibsiz).")
B.ST=s(["inconclusive","definitive","fabricated","predictable"],t.s)
B.a_w=new A.bx("Because the results of the first trial were ______, the research team designed a second experiment with a much larger sample to determine whether the treatment truly had an effect.",u.Y,B.ST,"Ikkinchi tajriba \"haqiqatan ta'siri bormi\" \u2014 aniqlash uchun kerak bo'ldi. Demak, birinchi natija aniq xulosa bermagan \u2192 inconclusive.")
B.Ti=s(["restrained in speech and manner","booked in advance","kept for later use","doubtful"],t.s)
B.a_i=new A.bx('The new student was reserved during her first week, answering questions politely but rarely offering her own opinions.\n\nAs used in the text, what does the word "reserved" most nearly mean?',"Choose the best meaning.",B.Ti,"Kontekst: savollarga muloyim javob beradi, lekin o'z fikrini kam aytadi \u2192 o'zini tutadigan, kamgap. \"booked in advance\" \u2014 so'zning boshqa (bron qilingan) ma'nosi, bu yerga mos emas.")
B.Tg=s(["reliable","loud","healthy","deep"],t.s)
B.a_6=new A.bx('After reviewing data from three independent laboratories, the committee concluded that the study\'s methods were sound and that its conclusions could be trusted.\n\nAs used in the text, what does the word "sound" most nearly mean?',"Choose the best meaning.",B.Tg,'"conclusions could be trusted" \u2014 usullar ishonchli \u2192 reliable. "sound" ning eng mashhur ma\'nosi (tovush) bu yerda emas.')
B.NU=s([B.a_d,B.a_k,B.a_s,B.a_O,B.a_o,B.a_w,B.a_i,B.a_6],t.vn)
B.a_U=new A.ef("wic","Words in Context","So'zning matndagi ma'nosi","\ud83d\udd24","Craft and Structure","Variantlarga qaramasdan oldin bo'sh joyga o'zingiz mos so'z o'ylang (o'zbekcha bo'lsa ham). Matndagi kalit so'zlarga e'tibor bering: 'although', 'but', 'not' \u2014 qarama-qarshilikni, ':' va 'because' \u2014 tushuntirishni bildiradi. So'zning eng mashhur ma'nosiga aldanmang.",B.NU)
B.SZ=s(["Specifically","However","Nevertheless","In contrast"],t.s)
B.a_j=new A.bx("Honeybees can learn to recognize individual human faces in laboratory experiments. ______, the insects learn to associate a particular face with a sugar reward and then return to that face again and again.",u.J,B.SZ,"Ikkinchi gap birinchisini aniqlashtiradi \u2014 qanday qilib tanishini tushuntiradi \u2192 Specifically.")
B.RW=s(["As a result","For instance","Even so","Similarly"],t.s)
B.a_J=new A.bx("Early telescopes produced blurry images because their lenses bent different colors of light by different amounts. ______, seventeenth-century astronomers often struggled to see fine details on the surfaces of planets.",u.J,B.RW,"Xira tasvir \u2014 sabab, detallarni ko'ra olmaslik \u2014 natija \u2192 As a result.")
B.Qg=s(["In fact","Therefore","Likewise","Finally"],t.s)
B.a_5=new A.bx("Many people assume that deserts are nearly lifeless. ______, the Kyzylkum Desert supports hundreds of species of plants, reptiles, and birds adapted to its extreme temperatures.",u.J,B.Qg,"Ikkinchi gap keng tarqalgan fikrni rad etadi \u2192 In fact (aslida esa).")
B.TD=s(["Subsequently","Conversely","For example","Nonetheless"],t.s)
B.a_E=new A.bx("The architect's first design was rejected because it was too expensive. ______, she submitted a revised plan that used locally produced brick and reduced costs by 30 percent.",u.J,B.TD,"Voqealar ketma-ketligi: avval rad etildi, keyin yangi reja \u2192 Subsequently (keyinroq).")
B.PM=s(["However","Thus","In addition","For this reason"],t.s)
B.a_t=new A.bx("Solar panels produce no emissions while they operate. ______, manufacturing them requires energy and raw materials, so their environmental impact is not zero.",u.J,B.PM,"Birinchi gap afzallik, ikkinchisi cheklov \u2192 zidlik: However.")
B.PQ=s(["Moreover","Instead","In contrast","Regardless"],t.s)
B.a_z=new A.bx("The study found that students who slept at least eight hours performed better on memory tests. ______, these students were also more likely to report feeling calm before exams.",u.J,B.PQ,"Ikkinchi gap yana bir ijobiy natijani qo'shadi \u2192 Moreover (bundan tashqari).")
B.Tw=s(["by contrast","for example","therefore","similarly"],t.s)
B.a_x=new A.bx("Some languages, such as English, rely heavily on word order to show who did what to whom. Other languages, ______, use word endings to mark grammatical roles, allowing words to appear in many different orders.",u.J,B.Tw,"Ikki xil tillar taqqoslanmoqda va ular bir-biriga qarama-qarshi \u2192 by contrast.")
B.OF=s([B.a_j,B.a_J,B.a_5,B.a_E,B.a_t,B.a_z,B.a_x],t.vn)
B.a_W=new A.ef("transitions","Transitions","Bog'lovchi so'zlar","\ud83d\udd17","Expression of Ideas","Ikki gap orasidagi mantiqiy aloqani aniqlang:\n\u2022 zidlik \u2014 however, nevertheless, in contrast, by contrast\n\u2022 natija \u2014 therefore, as a result, thus, consequently\n\u2022 qo'shimcha \u2014 moreover, in addition, furthermore\n\u2022 aniqlashtirish / misol \u2014 specifically, for example, in fact\n\u2022 vaqt tartibi \u2014 subsequently, then, finally",B.OF)
B.U1=s(["world;","world,","world","world and"],t.s)
B.a_B=new A.bx("The Aral Sea was once the fourth-largest lake in the ______ by the early 2000s, however, it had lost most of its water.",u.Q,B.U1,"Ikkala qism ham to'liq gap. Ularni vergulsiz yoki faqat vergul bilan ulash xato \u2192 nuqtali vergul (;).")
B.R6=s(["artifacts:","artifacts;","artifacts, and","artifacts. A"],t.s)
B.a_v=new A.bx("The museum's newest exhibit features three rare ______ a bronze mirror, a silk banner, and a painted ceramic bowl.",u.Q,B.R6,"Oldin to'liq gap, keyin ro'yxat \u2192 ikki nuqta (:). Nuqtali vergul va nuqtadan keyin to'liq gap kelishi kerak edi.")
B.Rl=s(["Warsaw,","Warsaw;","Warsaw","Warsaw:"],t.s)
B.a_H=new A.bx("Marie Curie, who was born in ______ became the first person to win Nobel Prizes in two different sciences.",u.Q,B.Rl,'"who was born in Warsaw" \u2014 qo\'shimcha izoh. U vergul bilan boshlangan, demak vergul bilan yopilishi kerak.')
B.NO=s(["cold, and","cold,","cold","cold and,"],t.s)
B.a_h=new A.bx("The engineers tested the new battery in extreme ______ it continued to work at temperatures as low as minus forty degrees Celsius.",u.Q,B.NO,"Ikki to'liq gap \u2192 vergul + and. Faqat vergul (comma splice) xato.")
B.QZ=s(["nutcrackers","nutcrackers,","nutcrackers;","nutcrackers:"],t.s)
B.a_I=new A.bx("Researchers studying ______ found that these birds can remember the locations of thousands of hidden seeds for months.",u.Q,B.QZ,'"Researchers studying nutcrackers" \u2014 gapning egasi, "found" \u2014 kesim. Ega va kesim orasida tinish belgisi bo\'lmaydi.')
B.P9=s(["world; in fact,","world, in fact,","world in fact","world, in fact"],t.s)
B.a_e=new A.bx("The festival attracts visitors from around the ______ many of them return year after year.",u.Q,B.P9,'Ikki to\'liq gap; "in fact" ikkinchi gapga tegishli \u2192 world; in fact,')
B.QP=s([B.a_B,B.a_v,B.a_H,B.a_h,B.a_I,B.a_e],t.vn)
B.a_R=new A.ef("boundaries","Boundaries","Tinish belgilari","\u2702\ufe0f","Standard English Conventions","Avval to'liq (mustaqil) gaplarni toping.\n\u2022 Ikki to'liq gapni FAQAT vergul bilan ulab bo'lmaydi: nuqta, nuqtali vergul (;) yoki \", and / , but\" kerak.\n\u2022 Ikki nuqta (:) dan oldin to'liq gap, keyin \u2014 tushuntirish yoki ro'yxat.\n\u2022 Ega bilan kesim orasiga vergul qo'yilmaydi.\n\u2022 Qo'shimcha izoh (who..., which...) ikki tomondan vergul bilan ajratiladi.",B.QP)
B.l7=s(["is","are","were","have been"],t.s)
B.a_f=new A.bx("The collection of letters written by the explorer during his travels ______ now housed in the national library.",u.Q,B.l7,'Ega \u2014 "collection" (birlik). "letters" \u2014 faqat izoh qismi \u2192 is.')
B.a_y=new A.bx("Each of the students in the robotics club ______ responsible for designing one part of the machine.",u.Q,B.l7,'"Each" \u2014 birlik \u2192 is.')
B.OX=s(["darkened","darkens","will darken","has darkened"],t.s)
B.a_N=new A.bx('When Mount Tambora erupted in 1815, ash and gases ______ the sky for months, contributing to what became known as "the year without a summer" in 1816.',u.Q,B.OX,"O'tgan zamondagi voqea (1815, erupted) \u2192 Past Simple: darkened.")
B.RS=s(["had repeated","repeat","will repeat","are repeating"],t.s)
B.a_c=new A.bx("The scientists published their findings only after they ______ the experiment three times.",u.Q,B.RS,"Tajriba nashrdan OLDIN takrorlangan \u2192 Past Perfect: had repeated.")
B.Sr=s(["were","was","is","has been"],t.s)
B.a_b=new A.bx("Neither the director nor the actors ______ aware that the camera was still recording.",u.Q,B.Sr,"neither... nor... da kesim yaqinroq egaga (the actors \u2014 ko'plik) moslanadi \u2192 were.")
B.Rz=s(["Dilnoza finished the marathon in under four hours.","the marathon was finished by Dilnoza in under four hours.","Dilnoza's marathon time was under four hours.","the four-hour mark was beaten by Dilnoza."],t.s)
B.a_g=new A.bx("Having trained for months, ______",u.Q,B.Rz,'Oylab mashq qilgan \u2014 Dilnoza. Shuning uchun verguldan keyin darhol "Dilnoza" kelishi kerak.')
B.a_u=new A.bx("The giant panda's diet consists almost entirely of bamboo, a plant that ______ low in nutrients, so pandas must eat for many hours each day.",u.Q,B.l7,'"a plant that ..." \u2014 that birlik "plant" ga ishora qiladi va hozirgi fakt \u2192 is.')
B.Qb=s([B.a_f,B.a_y,B.a_N,B.a_c,B.a_b,B.a_g,B.a_u],t.vn)
B.a_S=new A.ef("form","Form, Structure, and Sense","Grammatik moslik","\ud83e\udde9","Standard English Conventions","\u2022 Egani toping va orasidagi so'zlarga aldanmang: \"The collection of letters IS...\"\n\u2022 each, every, neither (yolg'iz) \u2014 birlik.  neither... nor... \u2014 kesim yaqinroq egaga moslanadi.\n\u2022 Zamonlar mantiqan mos bo'lsin: o'tmishdagi ikki voqeadan oldingisi \u2014 had + V3.\n\u2022 Gap boshidagi \"-ing\" qismi aynan shu ishni qilgan kishiga tegishli bo'lishi kerak.",B.Qb)
B.U6=s(["Bukhara's position on trade routes helped make it a major center of learning as well as commerce.","Silk and spices were the most valuable goods traded in Bukhara.","Scholars in Bukhara focused mainly on astronomy rather than medicine.","Merchants in Bukhara were more interested in religion than in trade."],t.s)
B.a_p=new A.bx("For centuries, the city of Bukhara sat at the crossroads of trade routes linking China, Persia, and Europe. Merchants arriving in its markets brought not only silk and spices but also new ideas, religions, and technologies. Scholars from distant regions gathered in its madrasas, exchanging knowledge in mathematics, medicine, and astronomy. As a result, Bukhara became more than a commercial hub; it developed into one of the most important intellectual centers of the medieval Islamic world.",u.h,B.U6,"Oxirgi gap xulosa: Buxoro savdo markazidan ilm markaziga aylandi. Boshqa variantlar \u2014 tor detal yoki matnda yo'q fikr.")
B.Rt=s(["Each arm can react to its surroundings somewhat independently.","Octopuses have larger central brains than most animals.","Octopuses cannot taste food with their arms.","Octopuses must use their central brain to grasp food."],t.s)
B.a_a=new A.bx("An octopus has roughly 500 million neurons, but about two-thirds of them are located in its arms rather than in its central brain. This unusual arrangement allows each arm to respond to touch and taste largely on its own. In experiments, an arm can reach toward food and grasp it without direct instructions from the brain. Researchers believe this distributed system helps octopuses carry out many complex tasks at once.","According to the text, what is one result of the way octopus neurons are distributed?",B.Rt,'Matnda: "allows each arm to respond ... largely on its own" \u2014 har bir qo\'l ancha mustaqil harakat qiladi.')
B.Tp=s(["A memory helps a nervous character begin her performance.","A character decides to stop playing the piano.","A grandmother teaches a character a new melody.","Judges criticize a character's choice of music."],t.s)
B.a_l=new A.bx("The following text is from a short story.\n\nNodira had practiced the piano piece for weeks, yet when she sat down in front of the judges, her hands felt like someone else's. She stared at the keys. Then she remembered her grandmother's small kitchen, where she had first played the melody on an old, out-of-tune piano while her grandmother hummed along. Nodira took a breath, and her fingers began to move.","Which choice best describes what happens in the text?",B.Tp,"Nodira hayajonlanadi, buvisining oshxonasini eslaydi va chalishni boshlaydi \u2192 xotira unga yordam berdi.")
B.SR=s(["A popular belief about the Great Wall's visibility from space is not accurate.","The Great Wall is the longest structure ever built by humans.","Astronauts can easily see the Great Wall from low Earth orbit.","The Great Wall was built using materials brought from far away."],t.s)
B.a_A=new A.bx("Many people believe that the Great Wall of China can be seen from the Moon with the naked eye. However, astronauts who have traveled to the Moon report that no human-made structures are visible from that distance. Even from low Earth orbit, the wall is extremely difficult to spot, because it is narrow and built from materials similar in color to the surrounding land.",u.h,B.SR,"Matn keng tarqalgan fikrni (Oydan ko'rinadi) dalillar bilan rad etadi.")
B.Pw=s([B.a_p,B.a_a,B.a_l,B.a_A],t.vn)
B.a_T=new A.ef("central","Central Ideas and Details","Asosiy g'oya va tafsilotlar","\ud83c\udfaf","Information and Ideas","Matnni o'qib, uni bitta gap bilan o'zingiz xulosa qiling, keyin variantlarni taqqoslang.\nXato variantlar odatda: juda tor (bitta detal), juda keng yoki matnda umuman aytilmagan fikr.",B.Pw)
B.U5=s(["a higher number of eggs does not necessarily lead to a larger adult frog population.","the frogs lay fewer eggs when streams are moving quickly.","heavy rainfall has no effect on the frogs' reproduction.","tadpoles survive better in fast-moving streams than in calm water."],t.s)
B.a_r=new A.bx("Researchers found that a species of frog in Panama lays more eggs in years with heavy rainfall. However, in those same years, fewer tadpoles survive to adulthood, because fast-moving streams wash many of them away. These findings suggest that ______",u.p,B.U5,"Tuxum ko'p, lekin kam itbaliq omon qoladi \u2192 ko'p tuxum hali katta populyatsiya degani emas.")
B.T2=s(["reading for pleasure causes teenagers' vocabulary to improve.","some teenagers read printed books for pleasure.","homes differ in the number of books they contain.","vocabulary test scores varied among the teenagers."],t.s)
B.a_7=new A.bx("In a survey of 2,000 teenagers, those who read printed books for pleasure at least three times a week scored higher on vocabulary tests than those who did not. However, the teenagers who read more also tended to come from homes with more books. Therefore, the survey alone cannot show that ______",u.p,B.T2,"Boshqa omil (uydagi kitoblar) ham bor, shuning uchun so'rovnoma SABAB-NATIJANI isbotlay olmaydi. Qolgan variantlar so'rovnomada aniq ko'rsatilgan.")
B.Sn=s(["the region's landscape or the settlers' trade networks were likely different in the past.","the settlers never ate fish.","the fishhooks were made only recently.","the settlement was built on a seashore that still exists today."],t.s)
B.a_P=new A.bx("Archaeologists excavating an ancient settlement found fish bones and fishhooks carved from bone, even though the site is now more than 200 kilometers from the nearest sea or large lake. The archaeologists concluded that ______",u.p,B.Sn,"Baliq qoldiqlari bor, lekin hozir suv uzoq \u2192 o'tmishda geografiya yoki savdo aloqalari boshqacha bo'lgan. Ehtiyotkor xulosa (\"likely\") \u2014 SAT uchun yaxshi belgi.")
B.NP=s(["gives the plants enough time to produce seeds before the cold returns.","prevents the plants from being pollinated.","shows that Arctic plants do not need sunlight.","means that Arctic plants live longer than other plants."],t.s)
B.a_m=new A.bx("Some plants in the Arctic flower within days after the snow melts, while similar species in warmer regions take several weeks to flower. Because the Arctic summer is very short, this rapid flowering most likely ______",u.p,B.NP,"Yoz qisqa \u2192 tez gullash urug' berishga ulgurish uchun kerak.")
B.Q1=s([B.a_r,B.a_7,B.a_P,B.a_m],t.vn)
B.a_V=new A.ef("inferences","Inferences","Mantiqiy xulosa","\ud83e\udde0","Information and Ideas","Matndagi dalillardan BEVOSITA kelib chiqadigan xulosani tanlang. Juda kuchli da'volar (always, never, proves) va matnda asosi yo'q taxminlardan ehtiyot bo'ling. \"Therefore\", \"suggest\" so'zlari \u2014 oldingi gaplarning mantiqiy natijasini kutadi.",B.Q1)
B.QS=s(["Since the program began, the number of cars entering downtown each day has fallen by 12 percent.","The bikes in the program are painted bright green.","Many residents say they enjoy cycling on weekends.","The city plans to add more bike stations next year."],t.s)
B.a_K=new A.bx("A student claims that her city's new bike-sharing program has reduced car traffic downtown.","Which finding, if true, would most directly support the student's claim?",B.QS,"Da'vo \u2014 mashinalar kamaydi. Faqat birinchi variant aynan mashinalar soni haqida.")
B.T1=s(["The library averaged 650 visitors on Saturday, more than on any of the weekdays listed.","The library averaged 410 visitors on Wednesday and 290 on Friday.","The library averaged 320 visitors on Monday.","The library had fewer visitors on Friday than on Monday."],t.s)
B.a_8=new A.bx("Average daily visitors at a city library:\n\u2022 Monday \u2014 320\n\u2022 Wednesday \u2014 410\n\u2022 Friday \u2014 290\n\u2022 Saturday \u2014 650\n\nThe library manager concluded that the Saturday programs attract more visitors than weekday activities do.","Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support the manager's conclusion?",B.T1,"Xulosa shanba va ish kunlarini taqqoslaydi \u2192 shanbani boshqa kunlar bilan solishtirgan variant.")
B.Rk=s(['"Library checkouts by students have doubled since the program began."','"The program uses books from several different publishers."','"Some students prefer reading on tablets."','"The program was introduced in September."'],t.s)
B.a_G=new A.bx("Zuhra argues that her school's new reading program has increased students' interest in books.","Which quotation from a teacher's report would best support Zuhra's argument?",B.Rk,"Qiziqish oshganini ko'rsatadigan dalil \u2014 kutubxonadan kitob olish ikki barobar ko'paygan.")
B.TG=s(["between 2015 and 2020, when the share rose by 12 percentage points.","between 2010 and 2015, when the share rose by 12 percentage points.","before 2010, when the share was already 31 percent.","between 2010 and 2020, when the share fell by 19 percentage points."],t.s)
B.a_C=new A.bx("Share of electricity from renewable sources in Country X:\n\u2022 2010 \u2014 12%\n\u2022 2015 \u2014 19%\n\u2022 2020 \u2014 31%\n\nCountry X has rapidly increased its use of renewable energy, with the fastest growth occurring ______","Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?",B.TG,"Hisoblang: 2010\u21922015: +7; 2015\u21922020: +12. Eng tez o'sish \u2014 2015\u20132020.")
