B.a_Q=new A.ef("evidence","Command of Evidence","Dalil bilan isbotlash","\ud83d\udcca","Information and Ideas","Avval aynan qaysi da'vo isbotlanishi kerakligini aniqlang. To'g'ri, lekin da'voga aloqasiz ma'lumot \u2014 xato javob! Jadval/raqamli savollarda: variantdagi raqamlar jadvalga mos bo'lishi VA xulosani qo'llab-quvvatlashi kerak.",B.RY)
B.TH=s(["It corrects a common explanation for a feature of old windows.","It introduces the main topic of the text.","It provides an example that supports the idea that glass flows.","It describes how modern glass is manufactured."],t.s)
B.a_q=new A.bx("Many people think of glass as a solid, but its atoms are arranged randomly, like those in a liquid. Unlike a liquid, however, glass does not flow at room temperature in any measurable way. Old windows that are thicker at the bottom were most likely made that way during manufacturing, not as a result of the glass slowly flowing downward over centuries.","Which choice best describes the function of the last sentence in the overall structure of the text?",B.TH,"Oxirgi gap \"shisha oqadi\" degan keng tarqalgan tushuntirishni rad etib, to'g'ri sababni beradi.")
B.Qy=s(["To describe how a student project helped reduce plastic waste","To argue that tourists should not visit historic sites","To explain how plastic bottles are recycled","To compare different methods of purifying water"],t.s)
B.a_9=new A.bx("A group of students in a small town noticed that many visitors left plastic bottles near the town's historic sites. The students designed refill stations where visitors could fill reusable bottles with clean water for free. Within a year, the number of bottles collected near the sites had dropped by nearly half.","Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?",B.Qy,"Matn muammo \u2192 o'quvchilar yechimi \u2192 natijani tasvirlaydi.")
B.Tl=s(["By noting that the benefits they describe may depend on the type of workplace","By agreeing that a four-day week increases productivity in every workplace","By arguing that rested employees make more mistakes","By claiming that no company has ever tried a four-day week"],t.s)
B.a_L=new A.bx("Text 1\nSome economists argue that a four-day workweek would increase productivity, because rested employees work more efficiently and make fewer mistakes.\n\nText 2\nA study of companies that tried a four-day week found that the results varied widely. Productivity rose in offices where work could be easily reorganized, but in hospitals and factories, shorter weeks often led to staff shortages.","Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the economists in Text 1?",B.Tl,"2-matn: natija ish joyiga bog'liq (ofislarda yaxshi, kasalxona/zavodlarda muammo) \u2192 1-matndagi umumiy da'voni cheklaydi.")
B.SE=s(["It presents an earlier view, explains why it was revised, and describes current practice.","It lists several earthquakes and their effects on cities.","It argues that skyscrapers should no longer be built.","It compares two cities with different building codes."],t.s)
B.a_M=new A.bx("Engineers once believed that tall buildings had to be extremely rigid to survive earthquakes. Later research showed that rigid structures can crack under strong shaking. Today, many skyscrapers are designed to sway slightly, using flexible materials and special dampers that absorb energy.","Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?",B.SE,"Tuzilish: avvalgi fikr \u2192 nega o'zgardi \u2192 hozirgi amaliyot.")
B.Pd=s([B.a_q,B.a_9,B.a_L,B.a_M],t.vn)
B.a_Y=new A.ef("structure","Text Structure and Purpose","Matn tuzilishi va maqsadi","\ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f","Craft and Structure","Savol \"nima uchun\" deb so'raydi: muallif bu gapni/matnni qaysi maqsadda yozgan? Variantlardagi fe'llarga qarang: describe, argue, explain, contrast, illustrate, challenge. Ikki matnli savolda avval har bir matnning asosiy fikrini alohida aniqlang, keyin ularni solishtiring.",B.Pd)
B.Qj=s(["The Ulugh Beg Madrasa was completed in 1420, more than two centuries before the Sher-Dor Madrasa (1636).","The Registan, a public square in Samarkand, is framed by three madrasas.","Both the Ulugh Beg Madrasa and the Sher-Dor Madrasa are located in Samarkand.","The Sher-Dor Madrasa is one of three madrasas that frame the Registan."],t.s)
B.a_F=new A.bx("While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\u2022 The Registan is a public square in Samarkand.\n\u2022 It is framed by three madrasas.\n\u2022 The Ulugh Beg Madrasa was completed in 1420.\n\u2022 The Sher-Dor Madrasa was completed in 1636.\n\nThe student wants to emphasize the difference in when the two madrasas were completed.",u.B,B.Qj,"Maqsad \u2014 qurilish vaqtidagi FARQ. Faqat birinchi variant ikki sanani solishtiradi.")
B.PE=s(["Mosses, which lack flowers and seeds, reproduce using tiny cells called spores.","Some mosses can survive being completely dried out for years.","Mosses absorb water directly through their leaves.","Mosses are small plants that can survive in many places."],t.s)
B.a_n=new A.bx("While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\u2022 Mosses are small plants that do not have flowers or seeds.\n\u2022 They reproduce using tiny cells called spores.\n\u2022 Mosses can absorb water directly through their leaves.\n\u2022 Some mosses can survive being completely dried out for years.\n\nThe student wants to explain to an audience unfamiliar with mosses how these plants reproduce.",u.B,B.PE,"Maqsad \u2014 qanday KO'PAYISHINI tushuntirish \u2192 spores haqidagi variant (notanish o'quvchi uchun gulsiz va urug'siz ekani ham aytilgan).")
B.O0=s(["Paper was invented in China around the 2nd century BCE, many centuries before the printing press was developed in Europe around 1440.","The printing press allowed books to be produced much faster than copying by hand.","Papermaking spread to Samarkand in the 8th century CE.","Both paper and the printing press changed how people shared information."],t.s)
B.a_D=new A.bx("While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\u2022 Paper was invented in China around the 2nd century BCE.\n\u2022 Papermaking spread to Samarkand in the 8th century CE.\n\u2022 The printing press was developed in Europe around 1440.\n\u2022 It allowed books to be produced much faster than copying by hand.\n\nThe student wants to present paper as a much earlier invention than the printing press.",u.B,B.O0,"Maqsad \u2014 qog'oz ancha OLDIN ixtiro qilinganini ko'rsatish \u2192 ikkala sanani solishtirgan variant.")
