B.SJ=s(['When Sevara was eight, she made her first pancakes. They were burnt on one side and raw on the other, but her dad ate them all and said, "Delicious!" From that day, Sevara was in love with cooking.',"She started watching cooking videos online and copying the recipes into a notebook. At first, she made lots of mistakes. Once she put salt in a cake instead of sugar! But she never gave up. Every weekend, she cooked something new for her family: Italian pasta, Japanese sushi, Turkish soup.","When she was thirteen, her school organised a cooking competition. Sevara decided to make a modern version of a traditional Uzbek dish \u2014 samsa with pumpkin and cheese. She was very nervous, but the judges loved it and she won first prize.",'Now Sevara has her own cooking blog with more than ten thousand followers. "Cooking is like magic," she says. "You take simple ingredients and create something that makes people happy."'],t.s)
